## Creating a New Project from This Template

Use [Copier](https://copier.readthedocs.io/) to scaffold a new package from this template:

```bash
copier copy gh:EED-Solutions/eed_package_template path/to/eed_my_new_package
```

Copier asks for:

- `project_name` — distribution name, kebab-case (e.g., `eed-my-new-package`)
- `package_slug` — Python package name, snake_case (e.g., `eed_my_new_package`); also used as the repository name and the `src/` directory name. Derived from `project_name` by default.
- `description` — short description for pyproject
- `github_org` / `image_owner` — defaults: `EED-Solutions` / `eed85`

Every hardcoded template name (`pyproject.toml` name + script, `src/` directory,
tests, README, ruleset sources) is replaced automatically.

After scaffolding:

1. Create the repository in the organization (or let `gh repo create` do it), push, open a pull request and make sure all CI pipelines pass.
2. Update repository settings as needed (e.g., import branch/tag rulesets from `.github/rulesets/`). For more information, see [this guide](https://eed-solutions.atlassian.net/wiki/x/BIA8Mw) (private access).
3. Merge the pull request and create the initial release (e.g., `0.1.0`).

## Updating an Existing Project

Projects generated from this template store their answers in `.copier-answers.yml`.
To pull in template improvements later:

```bash
copier update
```

